# Static-host security/cache headers for Voxel Craft's public Beta.
#
# Format: Netlify / Cloudflare Pages `_headers` file syntax (no build
# step required, picked up automatically by both hosts). If deploying
# elsewhere (GitHub Pages, S3+CloudFront, a plain nginx/Apache static
# host), translate these into that host's native header config -- see
# PUBLIC_BETA_DEPLOYMENT.md "Security headers" for per-provider notes.
#
# Deploy this SAME file to both the Community origin and the Runtime
# origin -- the header set below is safe and appropriate for either.
#
# Deliberately NO Content-Security-Policy here: this Runtime is a
# single inline-<script>, no-build-step HTML file (by design -- see
# RUNTIME_ARCHITECTURE.md). A CSP tight enough to matter (blocking
# 'unsafe-inline'/'unsafe-eval') would break the Runtime's own inline
# script and its Mod-execution model outright. Shipping a CSP here
# would require restructuring the Runtime into external script files
# first -- explicitly out of scope for this timeboxed deployment
# milestone. Documented as a deferred item, not silently skipped.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()

# index.html / community.html change on every deploy -- never let a
# stale cached copy silently keep serving an old version (e.g. a
# pre-Trust-Gate Runtime). Everything else in this repo (docs, SQL) is
# not fetched by the deployed pages at runtime, so a short/no cache on
# the HTML entry points is sufficient; no immutable/long-cache asset
# tier exists yet since there is no separate built-asset pipeline.
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/community.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
